= How to speak in public

Have a good idea is the first step
Is able to share to other is another step

Make this moment easier for us

== Purpose

- Conveying a message

== 4 pillars

- Choose a topic / What I want that peoples remember at the end
- Identify the audience (professionals ? Students ? Knowledge level ? Interest ?)
- Identify time limit (30 sec ? 30 min ? 2 hours ?)
- Identify key elements (What sould it be based on ? What to present ? What NOT to present ?)

Example: Roger Federer trains itself a lot to win ! It's the same for presentations !

== Preparation

- Plan
- Do
- Check
- Act

=== Tips

- Record presentation -> learn a lot about ourself

== On stage

- Be relaxed !!!
- Master:
  - The subject
  - Your body (75% of the message is transmitted by the body !!)
    - presence and body language
    - stand facing the audience
    - no hands in pockets
    - controlled body language
  - Your voice
    - don't talk too face
    - speak for the dunce (speak until the far persons of the room: include the all room)
    - repeat important points
    - leave silences for the recording (informations are saved in silences)
    - repeat questions, making sure every body hear the question
    - master your disaster words
  - Time
  - The audience
    - interact with audience to keep it !
    - attention
    - observation: the 7 dwarfs
    - interactivity (keep the audience !)
    - eye contact (I saw you ! I know that you are here !)

== Powerpoint

- Added value to the presentation
- More informations on what I'm saying than on the slides
- NEVER read the slides (we can make a silent moment to give time to read slides)
- Readability (careful to contrast)
- Keywords
- Image and illustrations vs text
- Font consistency
- Be aware to the presentation material (perhaps bigger fonts needed...)
- Get presentation mode !!!

We are the most important asset in a presentation is us !!!!
